<title>USA: TYPHOON TO WEAKEN TO TROPICAL STORM IN E.CHINA SEA.</title>
<headline>TYPHOON TO WEAKEN TO TROPICAL STORM IN E.CHINA SEA.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Tina was moving move north at 12 mph in the East China Sea, centred 100 miles south of Cheju, South Korea, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Top winds were 75 mph. The typhoon is expected to weaken to a tropical storm as it crosses South Korea during the next 18-24 hours, then turns northeast into the Sea of Japan as an extratropical storm. It threatens South Korea with moderate damage from wind and rain.</p>
</text>
